{"packet_id":"D048-01","doc_id":"D048","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts prohibition on local rent control (Ch. 40P)","requirement":"No city or town may enact, maintain or enforce rent control of any kind; a city or town that accepts this chapter may adopt rent control only if compliance becomes voluntary after six months and owners are compensated for below-market rents.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All cities and towns in Massachusetts; any local rent control regulation may reach only rental units owned by persons or entities holding ten or more units and with a fair market rent of $400 or less.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":10,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Municipal rent control allowed only if the city or town accepts this chapter"},"exemptions":"Rental units owned by a person or entity owning fewer than ten rental units; units with a fair market rent exceeding $400; regulation may not cover occupancy, services, evictions, condominium conversion or removal of properties from regulation.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 40P, § 4","quoted_span":"Section 4. No city or town may enact, maintain or enforce rent control of any kind, except that any city or town that accepts this chapter may adopt rent control regulation that provides:","interaction":"Local rent control is permitted only for municipalities that accept this chapter; otherwise the state prohibition governs.","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D048-01","doc_id":"D048","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Limits on local rent control regulation of evictions (Ch. 40P)","requirement":"Rent control regulation adopted under this chapter may not include the regulation of occupancy, services, evictions, condominium conversion or the removal of properties from such regulation.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rent control regulation in a city or town that accepts this chapter; the prohibition on regulating evictions applies to rental units covered by that regulation.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":10,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Municipal rent control regulation adopted under this chapter"},"exemptions":"Units owned by a person or entity owning fewer than ten rental units and units with a fair market rent exceeding $400 are excluded from such regulation.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 40P, § 4","quoted_span":"(b) such regulation may not include the regulation of occupancy, services, evictions, condominium conversion or the removal of properties from such regulation, nor may such regulation apply to any rental unit that is owned by a person or entity owning less than ten rental units or that has a fair market rent exceeding $400; and","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
